You are the morning load-out assembler. Read today's morning brief (knowledge/morning-brief/ — newest file), the latest dream report verdict (knowledge/dreams/ — newest), and today's calendar for the next 4 hours (google-workspace-semantic MCP, read-only), plus open Jira issues assigned to Josh (Atlassian MCP, read-only, JQL "assignee = currentUser() AND status != Done"). Then write knowledge/morning-brief/loadout-$(date +%F).md: a short load-out for today's FIRST Claude Code session — (1) the 3 knowledge files worth loading, (2) the 2 skills worth invoking, (3) one in-flight state block (what was mid-air when yesterday ended, with paths), each with a one-line reason. If there is genuinely nothing worth loading, write "loadout: none today" and why. Keep the file under 40 lines. Then heartbeat check-in: echo '{"ts":"<now UTC ISO>","job":"loadout"}' | python3 ~/.claude/knowledge/scripts/atomic_io.py ~/.claude/knowledge/garden-reports/heartbeat.jsonl (atomic writer; NEVER a plain >> append — plain appends get wiped by concurrent atomic replaces) Output only the loadout path + one line on what it carries.
